<h1>StudyHub documentation</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Learn how to launch StudyHub and use each feature of the desktop application.
</p>

<section class="notice">
  <h2>Start here</h2>
  <p>Follow the quickstart to prepare your computer, obtain the source
     code, and launch StudyHub.</p>
  <a class="button" href="/quickstart">Open the quickstart</a>
</section>

<h2>Feature guides</h2>
<div class="cards">
  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="/features/browse-courses">1. Browse courses</a></h3>
    <p>Explore the demonstration semester catalog and select a course.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="/features/browse-groups">2. Browse groups for a course</a></h3>
    <p>Find groups for your selected course and understand empty results.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="/features/view-details">3. View group details</a></h3>
    <p>Read a group's description, meeting information, and capacity.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="/features/search">4. Search by course code</a></h3>
    <p>Search with a full or partial course code and combine it with filtering.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="/features/create-group">5. Create a group</a></h3>
    <p>Complete the group form, set capacity, and correct invalid input.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="/features/delete-group">6. Delete a group</a></h3>
    <p>Remove a selected group or cancel the confirmation to keep it.</p>
  </section>
</div>

<aside class="notice">
  <strong>Session-only data:</strong>
  Create an example group to try these guides. Keep StudyHub open while
  you work, because groups are not saved after the application closes.
</aside>

